test_mcp_docker	Build and push	2026-10-22T05:45:55.9832976Z             "body": "Preserve the upstream stdio MCP endpoint and add a separate local batch/jobs companion with strict schemas, explicit origins, durable cancellation, bounded reporting and conservative factory ownership. Fix production packaging/dependencies and disable inherited publishing.\n\nLatest completed native75 at90e1c43:1,881 reported test passes/9 failures, plus Mac actual-Codex TIMED_OUT944 and three failed diagnostic controls. All17 non-soak jobs conclude. Five175-file installs,25 response-disposal cases, five20-run factory fixtures,12 route negatives and12 profile reset/isolation instances pass. Windows fixed CIM parity and suspended-frame page reuse pass. Linux/Windows actual clients complete1k (model0/owned0); Mac cleanup is known but deadline fails. Original Mac Chromium capture and Windows Firefox startup/input/retry/HTTP/lifecycle issues remain. Keep draft: this is not release-ready.\n\nCurrent follow-up uses the existing stop signal for public fetch/navigation/locator/screenshot APIs. Real held-close POST and locator controls first fail, then pass with API rejection while public browser isConnected remains true. No effect rollback or retry permission is inferred. A new independent23-step fixture checks all12 declarative types, all six locator forms, exact DOM effects and PNG/report/factory audits. Local action regression49 passes each Node20/22/24; Node20 also reports2 unexecuted WebKit pattern skips, while22/24 omit unmatched cases. WebKit is unexecuted locally. Screenshot quota/crash controls pass. Actual Codex1k36.238s/model0/owned0 and fresh175-file install pass.\n\nAn empty CIM snapshot now fails rather than certifying no survivors; the regression fails before, then graph/cleanup16/16 pass each Node20/22/24. Legitimate PID0/null timestamps/singletons remain. Existing launch-ownership assertion gains fixed safe result fields without changing its predicate. No matching/role/window filters, signal authority, policy, deadlines or transport defaults change. Prior unknown candidates and journal/permission debt remain unclassified/fenced.\n\nCurrent native76 head9591621 awaits full native validation. See docs/CODEX_EXECUTION_LEDGER.md and exact native75-* evidence. No main merge or publication requested.",
